<DocsLayout title="Export to Timetable" description="Send completed BurrowTime entries to Timetable with project mapping, an editable review, and safe retries.">
  <h2>Install the connector</h2>
  <p>Timetable export is optional. Install BurrowTime and its separate connector from
    <code>main</code>; this feature is not in the latest tagged release. Keep both
    executables on your <code>PATH</code>.</p>
  <pre><code>go install github.com/fabean/BurrowTime/cmd/burrowtime@main
go install github.com/fabean/BurrowTime/cmd/burrowtime-timetable@main</code></pre>

  <h2>Connect your Timetable account</h2>
  <p>Create a personal token in Timetable Settings. Get your user ID from
    <code>GET /api/me</code> with that token. BurrowTime saves the environment
    variable name, not the token. The default site URL is
    <code>https://timetable.bluedroplabs.com</code>.</p>
  <pre><code>export TIMETABLE_TOKEN='your-personal-token'
burrowtime timetable configure --user YOUR_TIMETABLE_USER_ID
burrowtime timetable projects
burrowtime timetable map 'client portal' TIMETABLE_PROJECT_UUID</code></pre>
  <p>For another Timetable deployment, add <code>--url https://your-host</code>
    to <code>configure</code>. Use <code>--token-env NAME</code> if your token lives
    in a different environment variable. The <code>projects</code> command lists
    accessible project IDs with their clients.</p>

  <h2>Preview, then upload</h2>
  <pre><code>burrowtime timetable sync --today --dry-run
burrowtime timetable sync --today
burrowtime timetable status</code></pre>
  <p>Sync selects completed entries from today by default. In a terminal, it
    suggests destinations for unmapped local projects, then lets you review
    descriptions, destinations, and durations before confirming. A dry run
    makes no uploads or receipt changes. For automation, map projects first,
    inspect a dry run, and pass <code>--yes</code> to upload.</p>
  <p>Use <code>--from YYYY-MM-DD --to YYYY-MM-DD</code> for an inclusive local-date
    range, or <code>--all</code> for all completed history. Nothing syncs in the
    background, and local frames remain unchanged.</p>

  <h2>How entries appear in Timetable</h2>
  <p>Timetable receives exact start and end timestamps by default. BurrowTime
    sorts the frame's tags into its description: <code>+PORTAL-42</code> becomes
    <code>PORTAL-42</code>. Timetable has no billable field in this API, so the
    export does not send one.</p>
  <p>Rounding is off by default. If needed, set <code>--rounding up</code> and
    <code>--increment 15m</code> when configuring, or override rounding for one
    mapping. Rounding changes only the exported end time.</p>

  <h2>Retry safely</h2>
  <p>Every upload carries <code>source=burrowtime</code> and the frame's stable ID
    as <code>external_id</code>. If a response is lost after Timetable creates
    the entry, rerunning sync sends the same request and Timetable returns the
    existing entry. A changed body with the same ID causes a conflict, which
    needs manual review. Synced frames are skipped on later runs; changes to a
    synced local frame are flagged rather than uploaded again.</p>
  <p>Timetable and Clockify can both receive the same local project. Their
    mappings and receipts are separate. Keep <code>integration-sync.json</code>
    when backing up or moving your BurrowTime data.</p>
  <p>See the <a href="https://github.com/fabean/BurrowTime/blob/main/docs/TIMETABLE.md">full connector reference</a>
    and <a href="https://timetable.bluedroplabs.com/api-docs/">Timetable API guide</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
